==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage operates similarly to the original, up until the Zuche jumpscare at the 50-seconds mark. Try to maintain as much ground before that point, since that'll make dealing with them much easier. Generic Zuche counters like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] will be capable of catching them while unburrowing. Afterwards, it's a straight shot to the finish.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The Zang Roos will pose the biggest problem here, bring Cat Cannon Recharge [[Cat Combo]]s to [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] each one as they arrive and burrow. You can then deal with them at a leisurely pace with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cats]].

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The Zapys are the only real threat as everything else either does not push or is highly limited. Send a fast unit to intercept Axoloty at the base, lure Zapy to the Cat Base so the restriction is not a problem. Kill it quickly with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]], and/or [[The Invisible Cat (Special Cat)|Groom Cat]] before the two Zapies stack up preferably.

